Multimodal retrieval
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

{% if model_name.endswith('-NVFP4') -%}
This NVFP4 checkpoint supports the ``vllm`` engine only and requires a GPU
with NVFP4 support, such as NVIDIA Blackwell.
{% else -%}
Supported engines are ``sentence_transformers`` (default), ``transformers``,
and ``vllm``. Select one with ``--model-engine``.
{% endif %}
Send ``input_type="query"`` for text queries and ``input_type="passage"``
(the default) for documents. ``prompt_name="query"`` and
``prompt_name="document"`` are equivalent. Queries accept text only;
documents accept text, one image, or one image combined with text.

Use ``image`` or ``image_url`` for an HTTP(S) URL, a base64 data URL, or a
local path on the Xinference server. Local files require
``XINFERENCE_MEDIA_ALLOW_LOCAL_PATH=true``. Remote images follow Xinference's
media address, timeout, and size settings. Lists preserve input order. For example,
send this body to ``/v1/embeddings``:

.. code-block:: json

   {
     "model": "<MODEL_UID>",
     "input": [
       "A text document",
       {"image": "https://example.com/page.png"},
       {"text": "A page caption", "image": "https://example.com/page.png"}
     ],
     "input_type": "passage",
     "dimensions": 512
   }

``dimensions`` accepts a positive integer up to the native embedding size.
By default, mean-pooled vectors are L2-normalized after truncating dimensions.
Set ``normalize_embeddings=false`` to return the unnormalized vectors.
The 32,768-token context includes image tokens. Audio and video are not supported.

The Transformers and Sentence Transformers engines require Transformers 5.20.0
or later and a matching PyTorch and torchvision pair (PyTorch 2.8 and
torchvision 0.23 or later). The vLLM environment uses
vLLM 0.32.0 or later with ``transformers>=5.17.0,<5.20.0``; use a separate
environment from the Transformers and Sentence Transformers engines.{% endif %}
